// Where the bank-sync service lives.
//
// Only the HOST is configured here. The scheme is fixed to https in
// FinanceApp-Info.plist, so a deployment cannot be misconfigured onto
// cleartext, and — just as practically — an xcconfig value can never contain
// "//", which this file format would silently read as a comment.
//
// The tracked default is a placeholder on the .invalid TLD, which RFC 6761
// reserves so that it can never resolve. A fresh checkout therefore reads as
// "not configured" rather than quietly dialling somebody else's machine, and
// CI needs no secret to build or test.
//
// To point a local build at a real deployment, create the git-ignored file
// Config/BankSync.local.xcconfig next to this one, containing one line:
//
//     BANK_SYNC_HOST = your-service.example.com
//
// Nothing tracked has to be edited, so a real endpoint cannot reach a commit
// by accident. The optional include is last, so the local value wins.

BANK_SYNC_HOST = finance-bank-sync.example.invalid

#include? "BankSync.local.xcconfig"
